273
00:14:21,420 --> 00:14:23,660
I took my visitors all over the house.

274
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:26,700
I bade them search, search well.

275
00:14:27,260 --> 00:14:29,400
I led them at length to his chamber.

276
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:32,900
I showed them his treasures, secure, undisturbed.

277
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:35,560
In the enthusiasm of my confidence I brought

278
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:39,060
chairs into the room and desired them here

279
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:42,660
to rest from their fatigues, while I myself,

280
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:45,720
in the wild audacity of my perfect triumph,

281
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:49,080
placed my own seat upon the very spot

282
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:52,580
beneath which reposed the corpse of the victim.

283
00:14:55,130 --> 00:14:56,770
The officers were satisfied.

284
00:14:56,770 --> 00:14:59,730
My manner had convinced them.

285
00:15:00,850 --> 00:15:03,150
I was singly at ease.

286
00:15:03,930 --> 00:15:06,950
They sat, and while I answered cheerily, they

287
00:15:06,950 --> 00:15:09,110
chatted of familiar things.

288
00:15:09,970 --> 00:15:13,090
But ere long I felt myself getting pale

289
00:15:13,090 --> 00:15:14,650
and wished them gone.

290
00:15:15,090 --> 00:15:17,310
My head ached, and I fancied a ringing

291
00:15:17,310 --> 00:15:19,890
in my ears, but still they sat and

292
00:15:19,890 --> 00:15:20,930
still chatted.

293
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:23,110
The ringing became more distinct.

294
00:15:23,410 --> 00:15:25,730
It continued and became more distinct.

295
00:15:25,730 --> 00:15:27,910
I talked more freely to get rid of

296
00:15:27,910 --> 00:15:31,770
the feeling, but it continued and gained definiteness,

297
00:15:32,210 --> 00:15:35,370
until at length I found that the noise

298
00:15:35,370 --> 00:15:38,010
was not within my ears.

299
00:15:40,910 --> 00:15:44,310
No doubt I now grew very pale, but

300
00:15:44,310 --> 00:15:46,690
I talked more fluently and with a heightened

301
00:15:46,690 --> 00:15:49,330
voice, yet the sound increased, and what could

302
00:15:49,330 --> 00:15:49,890
I do?

303
00:15:50,390 --> 00:15:54,150
It was a low, dull, quick sound, much

304
00:15:54,150 --> 00:15:56,850
such a sound as a watch makes when

305
00:15:56,850 --> 00:15:58,450
enveloped in cotton.

306
00:15:59,530 --> 00:16:01,750
I gasped for a breath, and yet the

307
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:03,050
officers heard it not.

308
00:16:03,350 --> 00:16:06,530
I talked more quickly, more vehemently, but the

309
00:16:06,530 --> 00:16:07,890
noise steadily increased.

310
00:16:08,310 --> 00:16:11,110
I arose and argued about trifles in a

311
00:16:11,110 --> 00:16:14,590
high key, and with violent gesticulations, but the

312
00:16:14,590 --> 00:16:16,110
noise steadily increased.

313
00:16:16,930 --> 00:16:19,810
Why would they not be gone?

314
00:16:19,810 --> 00:16:22,570
I paced the floor to and fro with

315
00:16:22,570 --> 00:16:25,450
heavy strides as if excited to fury by

316
00:16:25,450 --> 00:16:27,770
the observation of the men, but the noise

317
00:16:27,770 --> 00:16:28,690
steadily increased.

318
00:16:29,190 --> 00:16:31,070
Oh God, what could I do?

319
00:16:31,310 --> 00:16:33,490
I foamed, I raved, I swore.

320
00:16:34,090 --> 00:16:36,050
I swung the chair upon which I had

321
00:16:36,050 --> 00:16:38,130
been sitting and greeted it upon the boards,

322
00:16:38,310 --> 00:16:41,450
but the noise arose over all and continually

323
00:16:41,450 --> 00:16:42,430
increased.

324
00:16:43,010 --> 00:16:46,950
It grew louder, louder, louder, and still the

325
00:16:46,950 --> 00:16:48,910
men chatted pleasantly and smiled.

326
00:16:48,910 --> 00:16:52,350
Was it possible they heard not?

327
00:16:53,390 --> 00:16:57,770
Almighty God, no, no, they heard, they suspected,

328
00:16:57,870 --> 00:16:58,530
they knew.

329
00:16:58,950 --> 00:17:00,870
They were making a mockery of my horror.

330
00:17:01,330 --> 00:17:03,609
This I thought, and this I think.

331
00:17:04,349 --> 00:17:07,329
But anything was better than this agony.

332
00:17:07,890 --> 00:17:10,630
Anything was more terrible than this derision.

333
00:17:11,130 --> 00:17:14,650
I could bear those hypocritical smiles no longer.

334
00:17:14,849 --> 00:17:17,270
I felt that I must scream or die,

335
00:17:17,270 --> 00:17:21,589
and now again hark louder, louder, louder.

336
00:17:22,470 --> 00:17:23,990
Villains, I shrieked.

337
00:17:25,069 --> 00:17:26,630
Dissemble no more.

338
00:17:27,170 --> 00:17:28,250
I admit the deed.

339
00:17:28,390 --> 00:17:30,090
Tear up the planks here, here.

340
00:17:30,530 --> 00:17:32,510
It is the beating of this hideous heart.

341
00:17:36,410 --> 00:17:38,450
End of THE TAILTAIL HEART
